        "slug": "the-creative-to-ua-handoff",
        "title": "The Creative-to-UA Handoff",
        "content": "### Chapter Outcome\n\nAt the end of this chapter, you should be able to collaborate with UA as part of one learning system. You are not expected to become a media buyer. You are expected to understand the creative information that must travel with an asset, interpret performance feedback without overreacting, and translate a useful observation into the next batch of work.\n\n## The Creative-to-UA Handoff\n\n### A File Is Not a Handoff\n\nSending a file link without context creates avoidable confusion. UA cannot reliably evaluate the asset if they do not know what message, audience, concept, or variable it was designed to test.\n\nEvery handoff should include:\n\n| Field | Why UA needs it |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Asset name and version** | Enables accurate reporting and future retrieval. |\n| **Portfolio lane** | Clarifies whether the asset is an optimisation, exploration, or Go Wild test. |\n| **Concept and angle** | Allows concept-level learning beyond one individual ad. |\n| **Customer problem / audience context** | Preserves the relevance hypothesis. |\n| **Hook and primary message** | Makes the intended communication explicit. |\n| **Execution / format** | Supports taxonomy and comparisons. |\n| **Variable changed** | Shows what was deliberately varied. |\n| **Product-truth or claim note** | Prevents inappropriate use or unclear approval status. |\n| **Expected learning** | Tells the team what question the asset should help answer. |\n\nA clean handoff is a sign of respect for the work. It tells UA that the asset is part of a decision system, not content for content's sake.\n\n### Practical Exercise\n\nTake three existing assets and write complete handoff cards for each. Ask a UA person whether they could understand the intended learning without asking follow-up questions.\n"
