        "slug": "turning-feedback-into-the-next-batch",
        "title": "Turning Feedback Into the Next Batch",
        "content": "## Turning Feedback Into the Next Batch\n\n### Feedback Must Become a Decision\n\nA useful feedback loop converts evidence into a next action. The action should be specific enough for production and clear enough for UA to evaluate later.\n\n| Observation | Weak response | Strong next action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| A concept earns attention but the product is unclear. | \"Make it more engaging.\" | Keep the customer tension; move product truth earlier and test a product-demo proof. |\n| A winner is losing delivery over time. | \"Make five new versions.\" | Preserve the central tension; develop three high-leverage hook/visual branches and one new concept. |\n| An exploration asset has weak early business results but strong attention. | \"Turn it off forever.\" | Review expectation and destination continuity; create two proof-focused iterations and retest the concept. |\n| A creative converts but only in one execution style. | \"Copy the video.\" | Identify the message and proof mechanism; test the same concept through distinct visual formats. |\n\n### The Next-Batch Brief\n\nEvery next-batch request should state:\n\n- What was observed;\n- What is hypothesised;\n- What should stay constant;\n- What should change;\n- What output is required;\n- What would count as useful learning.\n\n### Practical Exercise\n\nWrite a **Next-Batch Brief** for three different feedback scenarios. Each must name the exact variable to change and the exact learning to seek.\n"
