        "content": "## Final Case: From Insight to Creative Learning Plan\n\n### The Capstone\n\nThe final case proves that you can connect the entire creative system. You are not judged on whether your output looks like a finished commercial. You are judged on whether you can make customer-led, product-truthful, visually distinct decisions and explain what the launch should teach the team.\n\n### Required Deliverables\n\n| Deliverable | Requirement |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Customer evidence** | Three observations from valid sources and a clear distinction between observation, inference, and hypothesis. |\n| **Customer tension and audience context** | One specific situation in which the product becomes relevant. |\n| **System of Ideas** | At least three distinct concepts, each with angle, message, hook, execution, and proof mechanism. |\n| **Creative portfolio** | A balanced set of optimisation, exploration, and Go Wild work. |\n| **Production pack** | At least one production-ready script and visual proof plan. |\n| **Launch handoff** | Complete concept/variable/learning documentation for UA. |\n| **Learning plan** | What signals will be read, what could be learned, and what the next batch would look like under different outcomes. |\n| **Trust / QA check** | Product truth, user respect, rights, and claim considerations documented. |\n\n### Presentation Standard\n\nYour final presentation should answer this chain without gaps:\n\n> What did you observe? -> What do you believe this means? -> What customer message should be tested? -> How will the concept look and feel distinct? -> What does the product truth require? -> What should UA learn from the launch? -> What will you produce next if the signal is strong, weak, or mixed?\n"
