        "content": "## Founder / Creative Lead Review\n\nThe final review is not a ceremony. It is a working conversation that confirms whether the creator can defend decisions with customer, product, and business reasoning.\n\n### Prepare Before the Review\n\nBring your complete final case and be ready to answer:\n\n1. Which observation is strongest, and why?\n2. Which part of your work is a hypothesis rather than a fact?\n3. What makes your three concepts genuinely different?\n4. Which element of your strongest concept is most uncertain?\n5. How did you avoid confusing effort with likely performance?\n6. What would you change after the first performance signal?\n7. What product-truth or user-trust risk did you identify and resolve?\n\n### What Good Feedback Looks Like\n\nGood feedback is direct and specific. It does not say \"make it better.\" It identifies a decision that is unclear, unsupported, repetitive, overproduced, untruthful, or disconnected from the customer. The creator should leave with a concrete first live assignment and a clear standard for the next batch.\n\n### Final Assignment\n\nSubmit your completed **End-to-End Creative Case** and present it to the founder or creative lead. The work is complete when you can explain not only what you made, but why it should exist, what it should teach, and how you would improve it.\n\n### Curriculum Completion Standard\n\nA Jr. Marketing Content Creator has completed this curriculum when they can reliably turn a real product and customer context into a documented, differentiated, product-truthful creative batch; hand it off with a clear learning objective; and use feedback to propose the next intelligent iteration.\n\nThey do not need to predict the winner every time. They need to build a system that gives the team more useful chances to find one.\n"
